From 81992e2108f0cde711fe2f9612380d14640d7a11 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:26:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/16] EXEC-MU-ACCOUNTS Phase 1 re-check C-P1A: failing tests
 of the auth-flow findings (no fix)

apps/edge-bff/tests/test_cp1a_phase1_auth_check.py, one test per finding:
- F1 throttle keys '<prefix>:<value>' in one scope collide with caller-typed keys (change:<user_id>, register:<email>)
- F2 password/reset answers 429 after 20 wrong codes only for an address with an account (enumeration)
- F3 an MFA-passed re-enrolment drops confirmed_at, so a password-only session enrols its own authenticator
- F4 a second registration in the same browser replaces the cookie of the first, whose code then fails
- F5 USERNAME_TAKEN uses no code try, so one code looks up any number of usernames
- F6 one registration by another browser plus its resends uses all 10 daily emails (against N4)
- F7 the sign-in body caps login at 200 characters while emails of up to 254 register
- F8 a reset by email code does not lift a sign-in limit anyone can reach by typing the login
- F9 the route walk accepts a hook route listed in HOOK_ROUTES whose handler never verifies

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015yBxadqbqnpdpSwmfCDQca
(cherry picked from commit d352cbae0d111bc342c031df48d37bbaf1e2d594)
---
